# Python backend

- Python 3.12, package `hero`, uv, `src` layout. Type hints on public functions.
- Pydantic v2 models are the schema. Use `model_validate`, not a hand-rolled dict check.
- Paths are `pathlib`. Writes are temp file + `os.replace` in the same directory.
- Numeric work is NumPy. No Python loop over point clouds.
- One heavy job at a time, in a process pool. Route handlers return quickly.
- Bind `127.0.0.1` only. Every `/api` route except `GET /api/health` requires `X-Hero-Token` and a local `Host`.
- Tests use `tmp_path` and an in-memory keyring. They never touch `Documents\2D Hero` or the real Credential Manager.

```python
# Bad
open(path, "w").write(text)

# Good
tmp = path.with_suffix(".tmp")
tmp.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
os.replace(tmp, path)
```
